# ipmt-markers.manifest: places that deliberately show explicit ::e / ::t markers.
# TAB-separated. Kinds: file (counts are minimums), fence (anchor = one exact line of the fence), line (exact text).
# Checked by: go run ./cmd-dev/ipmt-migrate -check-manifest -root .   See docs/dev-tools/ipmt-migrate.md
rule	event
line	docs/dev/parser.md	4. Type: `::e`, `::c`, `::t` (outside quotes; uppercase `::E`/`::C`/`::T` are rejected)	lists the type markers
file	docs/how-to-model.md	e=29 t=1	notation doc that shows explicit markers
line	docs/how-to-model.md	  - `thing` (**t**, `::t`): A persistent object or component, such as a service, container, file, repo, or engineer.	names the ::t marker of a thing, which is not the default
line	docs/how-to-model.md	- An unmarked node is an event — mark things (`::t`) and concepts (`::c`).	says an unmarked node is an event and things and concepts are marked
file	docs/inline-ipmt-colors.md	e=11 t=7	notation doc that shows explicit markers
line	docs/inline-ipmt-colors.md	| `t-marker` | the `::t` symbol | `t1 ::t` | `::t` | `#4d8a3a` · **bold** |	names the ::t marker token
line	docs/inline-ipmt-colors.md	- Legend line: the <!--ipmt:as-token:e-marker-->`::e` marker means an event (<!--ipmt:as-token:e-title-->`orange`), <!--ipmt:as-token:t-marker-->`::t` a thing (<!--ipmt:as-token:t-title-->`green`), <!--ipmt:as-token:c-marker-->`::c` a concept (<!--ipmt:as-token:c-title-->`blue`).	legend line that pairs each marker with its color
file	docs/ipm-modeling-tips.md	e=1 t=1	notation doc that shows explicit markers
line	docs/ipm-modeling-tips.md	Two or more `::t` nodes whose names differ only by a suffix	rule worded with the ::t marker
file	docs/ipm-rpc.md	e=4 t=2	notation doc that shows explicit markers
line	docs/ipm-rpc.md	| 0 | `ipmEvent` | Event node names and `::e` kind marker (default: orange; lighter `#ffaa55` with `hasAlias`; bold with `marker`) |	legend row for the ::e marker
line	docs/ipm-rpc.md	| 1 | `ipmThing` | Thing node names and `::t` kind marker (default: green) |	legend row for the ::t marker
line	docs/ipm-rpc.md	| 2 | `ipmConcept` | Concept node names and `::c` kind marker (default: blue) |	legend row for the ::c marker
line	docs/ipm-rpc.md	| 6 | `marker` | The `::e`/`::t`/`::c` syntactic marker (vs. the identifier of the same kind) |	names the marker token kind
file	docs/ipm-validator-rules.md	e=2 t=1	notation doc that shows explicit markers
line	docs/ipm-validator-rules.md	A `::t` node with no edges in or out.	rule worded with the ::t marker
file	docs/ipmt-ex/ipmt-examples.md	e=33 t=9	notation example that shows explicit markers
file	docs/ipmt-ex/ipmt-invalid.md	e=0 t=0	notation example that shows explicit markers
file	docs/ipmt-ex/mark-ex/examples.md	e=13 t=2	notation example that shows explicit markers
file	docs/ipmt-parser.md	e=4 t=1	notation doc that shows explicit markers
line	docs/ipmt-parser.md	- Types: `::e` (Event, default), `::c` (Concept), `::t` (Thing), and the undecided	lists the types and the default (event)
file	docs/ipmt-spec.md	e=76 t=32	notation doc that shows explicit markers
line	docs/ipmt-spec.md	or with the explicit `::t` marker:	introduces the explicit ::t marker
line	docs/ipmt-spec.md	The default node type is event. To specify type, use `::e` for event, `::c` for concept, `::t` for thing:	states the default type (event) and the markers
line	docs/ipmt-spec.md	Note: `::e` is optional because event is the default type: an unmarked node is an	states that ::e is optional and a thing needs ::t
line	docs/ipmt-spec.md	A node's identity is its canonical name alone, so `controller ::t` and `controller ::c`	shows identity is the name, not the marker
line	docs/ipmt-spec.md	Tooltip text must be enclosed in double quotes `"`. A type marker (`::t`/`::e`/`::c`) may precede the tooltip but is not required — the tooltip is the quoted string immediately before `::tip`. If more than one `::tip` is written, only the first is used.	says a marker may precede the tooltip
line	docs/ipmt-spec.md	Only one `::e`, `::c`, or `::t` type marker is allowed per node.	allows only one marker per node
line	docs/ipmt-spec.md	> Conflicting (`::e ::c`) or duplicate (`::t ::t`) type markers on a single node	explains conflicting and duplicate markers
